WEBVTT - Echoes of the Deep: Hydrophone Chronicles
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00.000 --> 00:03.500
[Deep rhythmic sub-surface ocean hum resonates]
Dr. Elena Rostova: We are lowering the hydrophone array 3,000 meters into the Monterey Canyon.

00:03.500 --> 00:07.800
[Water currents swirling softly around acoustic sensors]
Dr. Elena Rostova: At this depth, sunlight disappears completely. Everything we understand about this world comes from sound.

00:07.800 --> 00:11.200
[Distant high-frequency echolocation clicks of sperm whales]
Marcus Thorne: Picking up echolocation bursts at 14 kilohertz. Bearing 1-8-0 south.

00:11.200 --> 00:15.500
[Low harmonic vibration reverberating through underwater trench]
Dr. Elena Rostova: That's a matriarch pod communicating across dozens of nautical miles.

00:15.500 --> 00:20.000
[Bioluminescent flash sound cue accompanied by soft ambient hum]
Narrator: Welcome to StoryCast. Immersive acoustic journalism bridging science, sound, and human curiosity.
